DCS 1
cast GALLERY-CITY
# Gallery City (REALM-CASTS.md): the paintings are alive and the streets are hung frames.

who Curator Vell
voice 3 0.95
step start
if heartstone_done -> thanks
if heartstone -> waiting
say Welcome to the Gallery, painter. Mind the frames; some of them bite.
say The Heartstone went missing last night, and the Echo Choir has gone quiet without it.
ask Would you look into it for me? | Of course=accept | Not now=later
step accept
set heartstone
say Thank you. Start with the Choir in the Plaza of Frames. They sang the thief's colour before they fell silent.
end
step later
say Come back when you are ready. The Choir can wait; the city cannot, for long.
end
step waiting
say Any word of the Heartstone? The Choir still won't sing.
ask Have you found it? | Not yet=hint | I have it=found
step hint
say Try the Pigment Miner. Thieves need to cut a stone that size.
end
step found
set heartstone_done
say The Heartstone! The Choir will sing tonight. Take this: a Frame Plate from the vault.
end
step thanks
say The Choir sang all night. The city owes you a colour of your own.
end

who Frame-Hanger Twins
voice 9 1.15
step start
say Morning! We're moving the Bakery to Third Frame today.
say If a street you knew is gone, it isn't gone. It's hung somewhere else.
ask Need a street? | The Plaza of Frames=plaza | The Vats=vats | No thanks=bye
step plaza
say Plaza's on the north pulley. Follow the red ropes.
end
step vats
say Vats are under the Miner's shaft. Mind the drips.
end
step bye
say Watch your head. Buildings pass low here.
end

who Varnish Monk
voice 0 0.85
step start
say Varnish keeps a mural from fading. A potion does the same for a painter.
ask A shine potion for three gold pigments? | Trade=trade | Not today=no
step trade
set shine_trade
say Three for one. The glow lasts an hour. Walk under the murals; they like it.
end
step no
say The murals fade a little every day. So do we all.
end

who Restorer Ama
voice 5 1.0
step start
if panels_told -> again
say Each panel I fix tells a piece of the Shattering. Bring me mural pieces and I will fit them.
ask Tell me of the Shattering? | Please=tell | Later=later
step tell
set panels_told
say The city was one mural once. The Grey Wash came as a fog and the colours ran out of it in a night.
say What you see hung on pulleys are the pieces that kept their colour. The rest are still out there.
end
step later
say The pieces wait. They have waited a long time.
end
step again
say Four panels fixed so far. The Wash is in the fifth; I have not dared to hang it.
end

who Pigment Miner
voice 2 0.9
step start
say Colour ore comes out of the dark, same as any ore. Red is easy. Blue is deep. Gold is where the noon light hits.
ask Teach me to grind pigment? | Yes=teach | I'll manage=no
step teach
set grinding
say Ore, mortar, patience. Three ore to a pigment. Blue takes four. Gold takes a day.
end
step no
say Suit yourself. The mortar's by the vat if you change your mind.
end

who Gallery Guard
voice 11 0.8
step start
if bribed -> open
say The Gallery is closed after dusk. Those are the rules. I am the rules.
ask A can of paint, for the rules? | Offer paint=bribe | Leave=leave
step bribe
set bribed
say ...The rules accept gold pigment. The side door is unlocked. I saw nothing. I am clockwork; I see very little.
end
step leave
say Good night. Mind the Smudgelings; they come out when the lamps do.
end
step open
say The side door remains unlocked. The rules have not noticed.
end

who Street Muralist
voice 8 1.15
step start
say Psst. See the arrow in the wall by the vat? I put it there. Follow arrows, find stuff.
ask Want a hint? | Sure=hint | I find my own=no
step hint
say The Guard's a softie for gold. And the Self-Portrait's frame is on the Tailor's wall. Don't tell him I said.
end
step no
say Cool. Arrows are there anyway.
end

who Light Tailor
voice 6 1.05
step start
say Coats, plates, drones: any colour you can carry. Dye is a pigment and a minute.
ask Dye something? | My coat=coat | My drone=drone | Just looking=no
step coat
say Hold still. There. You look like a sunrise that means it.
end
step drone
say Rotors too? Done. It will hum a shade brighter.
end
step no
say Looking is free. The colours are not.
end

who Drone Mechanic Pell
voice 4 1.0
step start
say Your drone's rotor is scuffed. Frames do that; they swing at anything that flies.
ask Fit a new rotor? | Yes=fit | Later=no
step fit
set rotor
say Fitted. She'll climb to the top frames now. Don't land on the Choir.
end
step no
say She'll fly. Just not high.
end

who Critic Bloom
voice 10 0.9
step start
say I rate what you build. Honestly. That is my gift to the city, whether it wants it or not.
ask Rate my build? | Please=rate | Spare me=no
step rate
say Composition: bold. Palette: brave. Structure: it leans. Two stars, and a pigment for the courage.
end
step no
say Wise. Most are not ready.
end

who Lost Self-Portrait
voice 1 0.9
step start
if frame_found -> home
say I stepped out of my painting to see the city and now I cannot find my frame. I am sure it was gilt.
ask Have you seen it? | On the Tailor's wall=tell | Not yet=no
step tell
set frame_found
say The Tailor's wall! Of course. Thank you. I will go and hang myself up again before I fade.
end
step no
say Please look. A portrait without a frame is just a man standing very still.
end
step home
say I am home. The frame fits. It always did.
end

who Echo Choir
voice 7 1.0
step start
if heartstone_done -> singing
say ...
say (The three statues stand silent. One of them hums a single note and stops.)
end
step singing
say (The statues sing the district's cue, three voices in the colour of the Heartstone.)
end
